WEBVTT

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.910
Um, here's the script!

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.580
Sorry to bother you!

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.000
"Romeo and Julius"

00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:58.750
"Good Night, Theater"

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:02.450
"Good Night, Theater"
Okay, we'll be doing read-throughs
together starting today.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.660
You've all read through it on your own, right?

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.080
Of course!

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.290
All set!

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.580
I only have five lines...

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.660
Itaru, did you have a chance to read it?

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.080
Yup. Thanks for bringing it to me.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.120
I was half-asleep at the time.
Did I say anything strange?

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.750
N-No!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.700
Wait.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.950
Masumi, where's your script?

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.080
Don't need it. It's all in my head.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.000
What? You already memorized your lines?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.910
Yup.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.750
You're amazing!

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:35.250
All right! Let's start from the top!

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.580
There's a whole world I don't know out there.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:44.750
I want to see it with my own eyes someday.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:50.790
If we share the same dream,
there's only... one thing to do.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.830
Let's go on a journey together, Julius!

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.080
Er... We can ditch this cramped town

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.200
and travel the world!

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.830
You've got brawn, Romeo, and I've got brains.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.250
Ooh.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.910
Romeo, are you heartbroken?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.620
Don't worry about it.
There's plenty of fish in the sea.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.830
Any more and I take this as a declaration
of war against House Montague.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.450
Ooh! My God!

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:29.830
Julius, I promised to go on a journey... er...

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:35.540
Awkward. You keep messing up,
so it's hard to engage.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.290
It's our first time through. You can't
expect too much. Let's just get through--

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.540
You can't even read the script in front of you.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.540
Sorry...

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:46.120
And <i>you </i>wrote it but don't have your lines down.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.000
What?

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.040
Stop, you two!

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.000
Sorry! It's because I'm no good.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.830
It's okay. We're rehearsing to improve.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.870
Hey, Director?

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:06.200
I'm still not feeling well.
Can I be excused early?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.620
Sorry.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.580
It's okay. Feel better.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:21.160
Okay, I'll read Itaru's parts.
Let's resume from that last line.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.040
"Basic Japanese"

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.040
"Romeo and Julius"

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:02.830
One day, Romeo, the family's future
will hinge upon you. I--

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:03.950
"The town's."

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:04.870
Huh?

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:08.250
It's "the <i>town's </i>future," not "the <i>family's</i>."

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.040
See? You don't have your lines down.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.250
You know everybody else's lines, too?

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.790
Even an idiot can remember them
if they hear them every day.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:17.870
That an insult?

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:19.620
You're imagining it.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:24.160
Anyway, you're the writer. Aren't you
supposed to get your character?

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.000
Masumi!

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.200
You think I don't get my character?!

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.750
It's like you're reading the lines
without putting any thought into it.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:32.950
I just don't have the feeling in yet.
It's not 'cause I don't get my character!

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.290
Ends up sounding the same.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.500
What?!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.330
Tsuzuru!

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.500
Masumi, you went too far.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.870
Learn to be a team player!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.910
So you want me to suck like the rest of you?

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:51.450
Halt right there! You're both
oozing your tempers!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.000
You mean "losing your tempers"?

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.200
Calm down, both of you!

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.500
Let's take a break.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.370
What dense air!

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.160
Let's call it a day.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.410
We're moving slowly, so will you all
practice a little more on your own?

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:21.450
<i>Two </i>of us, you mean.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.910
Who do you mean?

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:24.500
Dunno.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.830
Sorry! I'm the one who needs extra practice.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.870
Sorry, I'm off.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:49.290
I want see awith own eyes somebray.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.160
If we share the same dream--

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.200
Can I come in?

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:02.250
How unusual. It's so late.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.290
What's the matter?

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:09.910
I don't wanna see his face.
Can I sleep here? I'll take the floor.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.620
Are you talking about Masumi?

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.540
What's his problem?

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:16.410
He keeps butting in even when
I'm trying to practice on my own.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.830
Is he? That's not like him.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.750
It isn't?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:27.250
Well, at school, Masumi's always on his own.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:34.660
People at school know that he won't talk
even if you go up to him.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.950
He got so attached to the director,
which was surprising,

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:42.750
but I thought he didn't care about us at all.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.540
Now that I think about it, when we started
run-throughs for <i>Romeo and Julius</i>,

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.290
he started butting in more.

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:50.000
I've got it! He's a <i>tsundere</i>!

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.750
He's <i>only </i>prickly.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:58.200
Masumi's always alone at home
since his parents are constantly abroad.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.540
Maybe he's not used to
interacting with other people.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:07.370
I can't imagine being alone in my house.
I have a ton of siblings.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:12.790
Even though Masumi says harsh things,
I think they're accurate.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:17.660
When it's my turn,
I get all nervous and mess up.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:24.330
It might be his way of trying to
make sure our performance succeeds.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:26.910
"Romeo and Julius"

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.200
"Romeo and Julius"
I don't believe he's that serious about acting.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:32.580
I don't believe he's that serious about acting.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.910
No matter. I won't let him have the last word.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:44.120
Let's prove him wrong and
start practicing in the mornings.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.200
I'll join you!

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.040
As will I!

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.450
Okay, meet in the practice room at six.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:56.000
Okay! We should sleep early today.
Tsuzuru, please use my bed.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.410
Er... well...

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:06.160
It's okay. I'll go back to my own room.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.330
Gotta tell him about morning practice anyway.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.580
That's true.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.700
Let's send word to Itaru, too!

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.910
Yeah.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.000
Itaru, are you there?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.450
I hear <i>click-clack </i>sounds.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:22.910
He's probably...

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.160
Dammit! Wanna piece of me?!

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.660
It's a robber!

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:27.580
A robber?!

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.250
Nah, it's probably--

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.910
We've got to help!

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:32.000
Itaru!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.000
Yeah! Ten kills!

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.200
Hah! Come back and challenge me
in 100 years, noob!

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.750
Itaru...?

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.950
I thought he was gaming.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.910
Ooh! Itaru's in relax mode. Japanese bum!

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:51.750
Hey... What do you want?

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:56.290
W-We decided to start
practicing in the mornings.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.000
What time?

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.700
We plan to start at six.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.580
Six? I'll think about it.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:08.700
O-Okay. We'll leave now...

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.120
Later.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.910
Did he... seem a little different than usual?

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:20.910
More than a little. That's a
pretty hardcore online game.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:25.700
<i>Ultimate Weapon 4</i>. With equipment like that
at level 124, he's gotta be a whale.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:28.080
A complete game addict.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.700
You're pretty bad, too, if you know that!

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:36.330
Think they'll both come to morning practice?

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.160
I dunno...

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.040
Good morning!

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.370
Mornin'!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.450
Good morning to you!

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.540
Masumi!

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.370
Wake up!

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.250
Morning.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:01.250
Itaru, you came!

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:04.950
Yup, stamina on my social games
won't go to waste if I'm up early.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:07.830
That's why you're always on your phone?

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:11.500
So the Itaru we saw last night wasn't a dream.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.290
Look, Julius! The sun's about to rise.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:18.950
Just as we promised that day.

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:21.870
We'll travel the world!

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:27.120
You got through that without messing up!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.080
It was really smooth!

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.450
It flows better now.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:34.660
I'm so glad! It's all thanks to you guys!

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:38.790
Yup. The morning practice is helping.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.660
Finally at the bare minimum.

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:43.500
Seriously, can't you say it in a nicer way?

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:46.700
Let's just call it the first step.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.200
That's right!

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.910
Let's keep at it just like this!

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:56.750
"21 Days Left"

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:03.830
At this rate, we won't have enough time!

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:16.370
Oh, Director. These are old costumes and props.

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:21.700
They're pretty shabby.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.950
I'm already looking for a costumer,

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:26.540
and I have a close friend
who can do stage carpentry.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.950
Don't you worry!

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:29.370
Thank you so much.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:31.540
It's nothing.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:35.370
By the way, how's rehearsal going?

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:39.160
We just finished read-throughs.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:45.040
I see. Can't expect the
original troupe's pace, huh.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.660
Original troupe?

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.000
Manager!

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.330
Yes?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.910
Can you contact any of the
original Spring Troupe members?

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:59.330
Let's go on a journey together, Julius.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:04.410
We can ditch this cramped town
and travel the world.

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:05.330
Sakuya.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:06.200
Huh?

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.790
You're in the wrong position.

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:09.910
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.660
Wrong hand, too.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:12.870
S-Sorry!

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.290
Sakuya, it's okay!

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:19.830
Oh! Bathroom break.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:22.330
He's definitely gaming.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.450
Let's go on a journey together, Julius.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.660
We can ditch this cramped town--

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.290
Whoa, whoa!

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.660
This a school play?

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.910
I can barely watch.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:46.290
Um... Sorry, who are you?

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:51.540
Huh? Oh, you the director's daughter?
All grown up now.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.200
Huh?

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:59.450
Matsukawa begged me to come
knock some sense into you new lot.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.660
Does that mean, you're--

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:06.330
Yeah. I'm Yuzo Kashima, one of
the original Spring Troupe members.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:08.750
Thought he was a yakuza.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:14.160
Get a move on and start!
I'll be your first audience.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.950
You should be grateful!

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.330
Y-Yes, sir! Thank you, sir!

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:37.910
Now I'll fetch the ingredients
for the potion for you, Julius.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:41.250
How many times are we going to go through this?!

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:45.410
Look, Julius! The sun's about to rise.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:47.410
Just as we promised that day.

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:50.870
We'll travel the world!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.160
What do you think?

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:04.000
Man, I wanted to stand up
and leave about 300 times.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.750
Friar, let's start with you!

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.040
Me?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:11.120
Don't try to be an actor in Japan
if you can't even speak Japanese!

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:15.580
Please don't say that! Citron's an
exchange student and is learning Japanese--

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.120
Learnin' the language is a different issue!

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:22.330
You'll distract the audience from the story
if you struggle with the delivery!

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:26.700
Next, Mercutio!

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:30.540
You're saying all your lines,
but there's no feelin'.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:32.870
Do you care about this script?

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.540
I wrote it!

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:38.750
Ah, that's why. You're complacent.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:42.120
You've gotta perform with the audience in mind,

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.000
else you're just doin' it for yourself!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.620
Wh--

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:48.200
Next, Tybalt!

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.410
I have nothing to say to you.

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:51.370
Huh?

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:55.290
If you're not motivated,
get off the stage. That's it.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:59.330
Next, Julius!

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:05.040
You keep gettin' distracted
by the director's daughter.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:08.620
You're not even that good.
Stop tryin' to be a hotshot!

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:10.580
What?

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:14.500
Your actin's dry!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.500
Even Masumi's not good enough?

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:23.000
Hah. You thought you'd get by with him?
Don't underestimate theater, punks!

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:26.120
Last up, Romeo!

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.750
Y-Yes, sir!

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:33.500
Hopeless. You understand nothin'
about theater despite bein' lead.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.450
Go back to square one.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:44.040
That's all for now.
I'll drop by again if I'm free.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.620
Annoying.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:50.370
Thank you for coming today.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:54.450
There's no knowin' how much Romeo'll grow
if he gets in the right mind set.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:55.580
Huh?

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:03.790
It means that whether he succeeds
or fails depends on you.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:09.330
Let me just say that as director,
you're at fault for this disaster.

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:14.080
It's because you're too lenient.
You better accept that.

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:20.660
Yes, I'll refocus and give it another shot!

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:21.830
Good.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:47.120
You think they're okay? What if it was
too harsh, and they decide to quit?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:52.290
They won't. I'm sure they'll come back around.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:58.830
Sakuya?

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:00.750
Oh, Tsuzuru.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:04.250
Where're you lugging all that to?

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:09.410
I keep thinking about
what Yuzo said and can't sleep.

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.200
You, too?

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:16.040
I was happy just to be on stage
and was satisfied with that.

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:19.750
But I wasn't thinking about the stage at all.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:24.790
I can't keep going on like this.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.410
You're not leaving, are you?

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:32.830
That's why I'm going to try sleeping on stage,
so I can understand it better.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:35.250
What?!

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.160
I shall join you!

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.000
Citron, too?

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.410
I'm ready to go!

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.370
Jeez, all right.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.540
Tsuzuru?

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:50.410
Let's drag Masumi and Itaru with us!

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:53.540
Yeah!

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:02.200
Thanks for coming, everyone.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:05.410
I don't care where, as long as I have my games.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.790
Why am I here, too?

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.290
You're here. Stop complaining.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:13.080
It's like training camp! So fun!

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:24.410
Hey, are you guys awake?

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:25.660
Yeah.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:29.160
What did you think about what Yuzo said?

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:31.910
It pissed me off.

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.540
Annoying.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:36.160
I thought he was pretty harsh.

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:38.200
Whipping us rough with love.

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:39.620
That just sounds wrong!

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:45.370
I thought he was being harsh at first,
but I realized it might be tough love.

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.870
Yeah, that!

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:53.660
The director also looked troubled
watching our rehearsals.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:56.160
Since we started our run-throughs.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:56.700
"Sakuya: Get more acting experience"
"Masumi: Watch more plays"
"Tsuzuru: Read different types of plays"
Since we started our run-throughs.

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:59.700
"Sakuya: Get more acting experience"
"Masumi: Watch more plays"
"Tsuzuru: Read different types of plays"
Masumi, you noticed, too, huh.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:03.660
So she's not satisfied with our performance?

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:08.750
Yeah, that's probably why she
wanted to give us a wake-up call.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:14.450
I see. You're probably right.
Gotta use that to improve.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:20.000
I watched my first play in elementary school.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:26.330
I was immediately engrossed,
and it made me want to be on stage,

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.290
to do theater like them.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:31.160
I kinda get it.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:36.700
I thought you didn't care
about acting or theater.

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:39.700
Even I have my favorite performances.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.830
How unexpected!

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:49.790
I want to know more about theater!

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:55.620
I want to get better at acting!

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:11.660
I wanna get better, too! I'll show Yuzo!

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.120
So loud.

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:17.540
I'll show you, too!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:18.870
You better.

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:21.580
I'll do my best, too!

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:23.830
Let's all do our best!

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:27.370
We're all in this together, huh.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:28.540
Yeah!

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:34.200
Romeo, you skipped a line.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.040
Sorry!

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:39.620
I'll try to direct the previous line
more towards Romeo.

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:42.750
Oh, that would help a lot!

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:46.080
Let's go again from the previous scene.

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.580
Right.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.750
"18 Days Left"

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.830
They're changing.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:57.120
At this rate, they should be fine!

00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:34.700
"Itaru Chigasaki"

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:36.080
"Itaru Chigasaki"
Itaru?

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:39.500
Yes, hello?

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:43.950
Hello, Director, I've been thinking a lot...

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:46.950
I'm quitting the troupe.
